This product includes original StrixOps software and assets adapted from the
open-source Strix project (https://github.com/usestrix/strix). Strix is a source
and behavioral reference; its Python runtime is not required by StrixOps.

The following assets are derived from Strix (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright usestrix / Strix contributors) and are used under that license:

  * The skills corpus (prompt/discipline markdown under
    src/strixops/skills/content/) is ported in substance from Strix's
    agent skill library, with skill names preserved for prompt stability.
  * System-prompt structure and tool guidance text follow Strix's prompt
    architecture.
  * The internal-pentest sandbox layer in containers/Dockerfile.sandbox
    mirrors the tool inventory of Strix's sandbox image additions.
  * Session management, context budgets and conversation compaction in
    src/strixops/engine/{sessions,context_budget,compaction}.py, the matching
    context settings, and tool-output bounding in src/strixops/tools/output_store.py
    are adapted from Strix v1.6.0. Engine/factory integration retains those
    behaviors while using StrixOps' OpenAI-compatible model routing.
  * Vulnerability deduplication and CVSS validation in src/strixops/report/
    and src/strixops/tools/reporting.py, child input-history inheritance,
    and image-history handling follow the corresponding Strix v1.6.0
    implementations. Sandbox image reading uses the OpenAI Agents SDK.
  * Coverage, threat-model collaboration, bounded child delegation, and rich
    dependency/source finding support follow selected reference behaviors,
    implemented within StrixOps' existing run state and event contracts.

The sandbox base image ghcr.io/usestrix/strix-sandbox is a third-party
artifact extended with internal-network tools for the shared web/internal sandbox.

